    description: "Swift: backtick-escaped names keep their backticks, so calls do not bind to them.\n\nREPRO: struct S { func `default`() {}; func run() { self.default(); self.`default`() } } - both calls go to stand-ins instead of S.default. A raw identifier containing a dot is emitted with the dot (`a.b`); downstream effect not checked. Found by PR 3 agent 6 (stable-id v16 branch, 2026-11-19) while sweeping Swift name extraction for WI-jujog: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/fast_smart_test_build_11172026/pr3/agent6/RESULTS.md."  # 015a
